The package.json file is a core file in Node.js projects. It contains metadata about the project and dependencies.

Properties in package.json
name: The name of your project.

version: The version of the project.

description: A brief description of the project.

scripts: Custom commands for running scripts, e.g., "start": "node index.js".

dependencies: Lists the packages installed (e.g., moment).

devDependencies: Lists packages for development only.

main: Entry point of the project.

author: Name of the project's author.